- No fragmentation: every concept has exactly one canonical representation and one code path.
  If two paths exist for the same concern, one must be deleted before the PR merges. [...] Less is more, but the target is not “fewer files at any cost.” The target is:

- fewer public concepts;
- fewer app-facing lifecycle recipes;
- fewer read/write doors;
- fewer hidden defaults;
- fewer native-owned protocol decisions;
- fewer duplicate sources of truth.
